  "crew": [
    {
      "name": "Christian Santalucía",
      "avatar": "/media/media::image::c::7579668770::vessel::d5cc24c7-fe8c-11ed-889f-43d4bb723744::assets::ec2217c0-867c-11f1-9ab0-d9ff5d8a2bbc/{imageVariant}",
      "role": "Captain",
      "bio": "Sail and Work Experience\nChristian is an experienced yacht captain with over 20 years in the yachting industry, specialising in luxury sailing yachts from 60–125ft. He has commanded prestigious yachts including S/Y AYNI (Oyster 885), where he managed Mediterranean and Caribbean seasons as well as a transatlantic crossing, overseeing all vessel operations, owner liaison, maintenance planning and budgets. He has also served as Relief Captain onboard S/Y KAILUA (Sunreef 74), managing high-end charter operations, and has captained a variety of Oyster, Lagoon and custom sailing yachts in both private and charter programmes. Earlier roles include Captain of S/Y BEATOO and First Mate aboard S/Y CHALLENGER 93, building extensive offshore, transatlantic and leadership experience.\n\nJob Description\nThe Captain is responsible for navigation, safety, the overall running and financial management of the vessel, crew and guests. He ensures the safe and efficient operation of the yacht at all times, including compliance with all safety procedures and regulations. He takes care of adhering to flag regulations, port state and local laws and regulations, and manages the crew to ensure adherence to, and a full understanding of, the vessel’s policies. He provides daily leadership for the crew and encourages teamwork, individual growth and personal development by delegating duties and supervising all crew tasks.\n\nLicences and Qualifications\n•\tRYA Yachtmaster Ocean (Commercially Endorsed) \n•\tMCA GMDSS GOC \n•\tSTCW \n•\tAdvanced Fire Fighting \n•\tMedical First Aid \n•\tAEC / AEC1 \n•\tHELM \n•\tECDIS \n•\tNavigation & Radar \n•\tENG1 \n•\tChief Mate <3000GT (in progress) \n\nLanguages\nSpanish, English\n\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Casey De Lange",
      "avatar": "/media/media::image::c::7579668770::vessel::d5cc24c7-fe8c-11ed-889f-43d4bb723744::assets::ab8fd480-867d-11f1-8f44-07f22d6f5f17/{imageVariant}",
      "role": "Captain",
      "bio": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "Chris-Mare Fourie",
      "avatar": "/media/media::image::c::7579668770::vessel::d5cc24c7-fe8c-11ed-889f-43d4bb723744::assets::d17425c0-867d-11f1-b8bb-4f5a34ce4dae/{imageVariant}",
      "role": "Captain",
      "bio": "Sail and Work Experience\nChris-Mare is a service-driven hospitality professional with experience in both shoreside hospitality and the superyacht industry. She has completed temporary Deck/Stew positions onboard M/Y KORU (50m) and M/Y SYMPHONY (101m), assisting with both interior and deck operations, including housekeeping, laundry, ironing, inventory management and maintaining the vessel's presentation. Earlier experience aboard a fishing vessel involved deck operations, fishing gear handling, cleaning, maintenance and catch management. Ashore, she worked as a receptionist at Club Mykonos Langebaan, delivering professional guest services, and as a conveyancer at PP Smit Attorneys, developing strong organisational and administrative skills.\n\nJob Description\nA Deck/Stew is responsible for supporting both the deck and interior departments to ensure the yacht is maintained to the highest standards. Duties include housekeeping, laundry, guest service, detailing, line handling, washdowns, assisting with docking operations, tender preparation and maintaining both guest and crew areas. The role requires flexibility, attention to detail and a proactive approach to supporting guests and crew.\n\nLicences and Qualifications\n•\tSTCW \n•\tSAMSA Medical \n•\tRYA Practical Sailing Course \n•\tLevel 2 Food Safety \n•\tStewardess Course \n\nLanguages\nEnglish\n"
    }
  ],
